{
    "background_story": "In a sun-dappled forest, a tiny beetle named Dearest lived a life of quiet dedication. As a member of the Cleridae family, she was a checkered beetle with a distinctive black and yellow pattern. Dearest spent her days scavenging for pollen and nectar, but her true passion was caring for her young. She would often venture into the underbrush, searching for the perfect twigs and leaves to craft a safe and cozy nest. Dearest's Cleridae instincts drove her to be a devoted parent, and she spent hours grooming and protecting her larvae. As they grew, she taught them the ways of the forest, showing them which flowers to visit and how to avoid predators. Dearest's selfless love and dedication to her family made her a beloved figure in the forest community.",
